# MDP changelog
{.lead} All notable changes, following Keep a Changelog and Semantic Versioning.

This is a presentation distillation of the changelog. The authoritative, full history lives in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).

---

## Unreleased

Nothing yet.

---

## 0.7.0

### Added

- **Body images.** `![alt](src)` now renders. A paragraph that is solely an image becomes a locked-size figure per form (the same asset-slot contract as `brand-logo`); mixed into running text, the same syntax stays inline as a small image. An unsafe `src` drops the image entirely rather than emitting a broken one.

---

## 0.5.0

### Added

- **Plan form.** A fifth interactive form, `plan`, renders an implementation plan as collapsible phases (each `---` section a `<details>`), the `{.lead}` as the goal, and `mdp:tasks` checklists driving a live progress meter. Reads the block set exactly as `page` does.
- **`mdp:tasks` block.** A status-aware checklist directive: `- [x]` done, `- [~]` in progress, `- [ ]` to-do. Renders in every artifact and feeds the `plan` form's progress meter.
- **Plan-mode preview.** A `/mdp-preview-plan` command and a project `PostToolUse` hook on `ExitPlanMode` render a Claude Code plan as the `plan` form via `scripts/preview-plan.mjs` (wraps the plan in MDP frontmatter, lifts task runs into `mdp:tasks`, splits a phase per `##`). Deterministic and read-only; never edits the plan.
- **Extension examples + a live showcase.** Three curated, zero-dependency, deterministic reference packages under `extensions/` (`mdp-block-status`, `mdp-block-spec-sheet`, `mdp-artifact-resume`), each with tests and an offline demo, gated in CI by `scripts/check-extensions.mjs` (tests, demo, determinism, engine-drift). The site gains an Extensions showcase running the real modules in `srcDoc` iframes, plus a "Build an extension" docs page.

### Fixed

- **Scaffolder doc gap.** Block wiring now documents `content-blocks.mjs`, so a scaffolded block renders inside the interactive forms, not only the static artifacts.

---

## 0.4.0

### Added

- **Send to Slack.** A new `mdp_send_slack` MCP tool (`mdp-mcp`) compiles a source and uploads the self-contained HTML artifact to a Slack channel as a file, via Slack's external-upload flow. Auth is a bot token in `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` (scope `files:write`); the channel is the `channel` argument or `MDP_SLACK_CHANNEL`. Any single form. Slack shows the `.html` as a downloadable file, not an inline render; opening it shows the full design, interactive forms included. Zero new dependencies.

---

## 0.3.1

### Fixed

- **The `mdp:diagram` tree layout** renders node names instead of their bare ids.

### Changed

- **The theme accent reads more boldly.** Accent-text link underlines thicken to 2px, inline `code` sits on an accent-tinted chip, the title masthead rule grows from a 3px hairline to a 4px bar, and list markers take the secondary accent. Still meaning-spot accents, so the design lock holds.

---

## 0.3.0

The engine, server, and scaffolder are now published to npm.

```mdp:stats
Engine: mdp-compiler
MCP server: mdp-mcp
Scaffolder: create-mdp-extension
Curated themes: 11
```

### Added

- **Interactive forms**: scroll, accordion, tabs, and stepper. Each compiles the same source into a different navigation experience, degrades to readable HTML with no JavaScript, and keeps WCAG AA contrast and keyboard navigation.
- **Timeline, FAQ, and pricing blocks**: `mdp:timeline` renders a vertical sequence of steps on an accent rail; `mdp:faq` renders question-answer pairs as native disclosure elements; `mdp:pricing` renders priced tiers as a locked card grid (the priced sibling of compare). All render across every form.
- **Custom brand color**: `brand-accent` (one hex) derives a full WCAG-AA accent set. An optional `brand-accent-2` adds a secondary accent in engine-chosen spots. `brand-font` picks the body family from a closed set of system stacks.
- **Published to npm**: `npm i mdp-compiler` to embed the engine, `npx -y mdp-mcp` for the MCP server, and `npm create mdp-extension` to scaffold a block or artifact.
- **An MCP server** (`mdp-mcp`) so any MCP host can compile MDP. It exposes `mdp_compile`, `mdp_present`, and `mdp_validate`, plus `mdp://spec` and `mdp://example/*` resources.
- **Five more themes**, bringing the curated set to eleven: ocean, forest, terracotta, coral, and plum. The set is now ordered as a spectrum, every accent WCAG-AA verified.
- **An AA-conformance test** (`npm test`) that compiles the real token CSS for every theme and asserts the contrast guarantees, so a future theme cannot regress accessibility.
- **A visual theme picker** in the playground, reading colors from a new `THEME_SWATCHES` export so the swatches never drift from the real accents.

### Changed

- The engine package was renamed from `@mdp/core` to `mdp-compiler` for its npm publish.
- The masthead now carries the theme accent (an accent-colored kicker and a short rule under the title) in all three artifacts, meaning-spot accents, so the design lock is unchanged.
- A hub and live playground at barmoshe.github.io/mdp, deployed to GitHub Pages, bundling the real engine and carrying the full documentation.
- A Codex plugin, self-contained in `codex/`, exposing an `mdp` skill that auto-triggers on "show this", "make a deck", and similar.

---

## 0.2.0

### Added

- **A color and theme system.** The `theme` field is wired to a curated set selected by name: studio (the default), teal, amber, violet, rose, and mono. An unknown theme falls back to studio.
- **A semantic accent token set**: a two-shade system tuned to pass WCAG AA in light and dark. The accent appears only in meaning-spots: links, the compare button, the recommendation callout, stat figures, the active slide dot, and flow arrows.
- **A Claude Code plugin** (this repo is the marketplace): a self-contained `/mdp` command that auto-triggers on "show this", "make a deck", and similar.
- The CLI gained `--open [artifact]`, `--out <dir>`, and `--only <artifact>`.
- The slides deck gained a fullscreen toggle, a print-to-PDF stylesheet, space-bar advance, and a keyboard hint.

### Changed

- Warmed the neutral ramp (a warm off-white background and near-black ink instead of pure white and black) so the default reads designed, not stark.

---

## 0.0.0

Initial public release. The spike that proves the core claim.

### Added

- A dependency-free Node ESM engine: one `.mdp` source compiles to three artifacts (page, slides, flyer).
- Blocks: `mdp:stats`, `mdp:compare`, `mdp:flow`, and `:::callout` (note, tip, cost, recommendation, warning).
- Line roles `{.lead}` and `{.cite}`, and right-to-left support via `lang` and `dir`.
- A single locked "studio" theme, and deterministic output: two builds of the same source are byte-identical.
